1
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:05,000
A second opinion only
helps if it's independent.

2
00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:09,300
The reviewer checks the same
mapping separately from the advisor.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:12,200
So if the two agree,
that's two separate looks,

4
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:14,200
not one opinion repeated.

5
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:16,180
The result opens with its label.

6
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:20,760
Then comes the outcome, such as
challenged or evidence incomplete,

7
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:25,160
followed by a short
summary, its concerns, its

8
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:25,820
uncertainty,

9
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:30,620
and your next step. For a clearing
account, expect a challenge.

10
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:35,380
A permitted target class isn't proof
of the account's business purpose and

11
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:38,640
without its settlement history, the
reviewer can't choose the treatment.

12
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:42,080
It's built so that unresolved
evidence never gets a clean review.

13
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:46,480
Now compare the two. If they
agree, you have support, not proof.

14
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:49,320
If they disagree, that's
your signal to look harder.

15
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:53,860
Inspect the source purpose and
settlement history or ask a qualified

16
00:00:53,860 --> 00:00:56,910
accountant. A second
opinion is not approval.

17
00:00:57,450 --> 00:01:01,310
When you're satisfied, approve,
change or reject the mapping

18
00:01:01,310 --> 00:01:03,390
and it's recorded under your name.
